  "line": "Hebron is an ancient city in Judah's hill country where Abraham lived and buried Sarah, which became Caleb's inheritance, and where David first became king.",
  "moments": [
    {
      "title": "Abram Settles at Hebron",
      "text": "Abram moved his tent to live near the Oaks of Mamre at Hebron. There he built an altar to the LORD.",
      "passage": "Genesis 13:17-18"
    },
    {
      "title": "Sarah Dies at Hebron",
      "text": "Sarah died in Kiriath-arba, which is Hebron. Abraham mourned for her and then asked the Hittites for a burial site.",
      "passage": "Genesis 23:1-4"
    },
    {
      "title": "Hebron Given to Caleb",
      "text": "Joshua blessed Caleb son of Jephunneh and gave him Hebron as his inheritance. It still belonged to Caleb's family because he wholly followed the LORD.",
      "passage": "Joshua 14:13-15"
    },
    {
      "title": "David Made King of Judah",
      "text": "David asked the LORD where to go, and the LORD said, \"To Hebron.\" The men of Judah came there and anointed him king over Judah.",
      "passage": "2 Samuel 2:1-4"
    },
    {
      "title": "David Made King of Israel",
      "text": "All the tribes of Israel came to David at Hebron. The elders made a covenant with him before the LORD and anointed him king over Israel.",
      "passage": "2 Samuel 5:1-5"
    }
  ],
